  "notes": "たむろする (also written {屯|たむろ}する) often carries a slightly negative connotation, implying idle gathering that may be unwelcome or suspicious.\n\nCommon contexts:\n- Groups of young people hanging out with no clear purpose\n- Delinquents or suspicious people loitering\n- People gathering without permission\n\nRelated expressions:\n- たまる (to gather - more neutral)\n- ぶらつく (to wander around - more active movement)\n- {溜|た}まり{場|ば} (hangout spot)",
